{"objects":[{"id":"flow","instance":"instance--b96dad5f-c519-5a1f-a718-912ca4a86c02","objects":["attack-action--1","attack-action--2","attack-action--3","attack-action--4","attack-action--5","attack-action--6","attack-action--7","attack-condition--1","attack-condition--2","attack-condition--3","attack-operator--1","software--1","user-account--1","instance--ea69be26-6559-52d4-8479-a0e32478e751","instance--acb605f3-8c48-56e9-bbf0-b21c54c1519f","process--1","instance--d562b69c-9a04-5f30-a5ee-3888fe0b887b","url--1","instance--8db41f38-2bcf-57f1-9329-014926391213","instance--e4f1265c-0d37-5abf-962e-f3c62b611a74","software--3","user-account--2","instance--ad1f125b-7701-5e9d-b869-79f40471648d","instance--dba76cba-ac10-53fc-8651-9c93dbcacdf3","instance--447a27ab-1541-5ade-b50d-bd1caecded2d","instance--83a2fc23-76ae-57c8-8fe5-a6179220aa87","instance--b6d82c28-0a68-5c6f-b058-c1e072f51852","instance--2ed631bc-5855-5c59-80fa-4925353c85a4","instance--56da8838-1109-5fce-9d89-7b3ec32d7010","instance--714f6cb9-bdb0-5e83-914a-3c8158d9f2de","instance--3ace54e2-1a43-5724-944b-c4b01d63d9e6","instance--e1fdbfcc-98c5-5401-a510-7f70aaad43ca","instance--d110b130-8c28-5cb4-98a0-76aaa8233093","instance--f64caa83-12dd-5204-a53f-519db6b69a9d","instance--fbf23322-e842-589b-a6e4-0d8af5704e8c","instance--465c895a-15c7-553e-ba1a-16498ce7bbe9","instance--9e41bc14-7da4-59c9-923f-256bded0dde5","instance--9d3f89be-694d-59a0-8244-5b93d5250ad4","instance--958b80fd-829a-511c-b49f-68736d6d8cca","instance--39107eda-f26f-57e3-a17f-9ce0cfe35002","instance--ccb01989-199a-5448-b51a-5828c66a7366","instance--f72c1729-3e7b-5c89-a3d7-54a4bd254178","instance--2c15d2a3-b722-5fc5-a814-f5df26ef48d5","instance--5295ddaf-b8df-5d9a-91ea-bc200f5badbe"],"properties":[["name","Kerberoast TGS ticket cracking flow"],["description","This post covers another type of Kerberos attack that involves Kerberos TGS service ticket cracking using Kerberoast."],["scope","incident"],["author",[["name","Sean Metcalf"]]],["external_references",[["item-1",[["source_name","adsecurity.org"],["url","https://adsecurity.org/?p=2293"]]]]]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--ad592d05-6969-5b51-98a8-1ad9b6aab896","120":"instance--5850a8f4-8241-5e73-9bf0-dcd376cd5025","150":"instance--0da1498f-3beb-5916-a249-e0410a4a81e4","180":"instance--d3632784-7391-5a29-83e2-edab51db56c6","210":"instance--8bc47ca5-ca73-5a04-a9ea-918608f10871","240":"instance--6546eef6-c5ad-516e-a417-89916e651648","270":"instance--244e5a69-f465-564e-9d2c-93d4da44fc57","30":"instance--6a1fca3c-fdb6-536a-bbea-61ac2349a700","300":"instance--043a5b44-2864-5565-abce-1909204e5485","330":"instance--e10eb918-2b0b-56f4-9c82-f345ce21276c","60":"instance--33a99d1b-dad8-51f6-be74-e1614db9151b","90":"instance--380c79e9-b1eb-547c-bf01-a011db1201c1"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--1","properties":[["name","Scan SPNs for services"],["description","Once the attacker has a list of Service Principal Names (SPNs) associated with service accounts, these SPNs can be used to request Kerberos TGS service tickets useful for offline TGS password cracking."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0006","technique":"T1558.003"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--4f4d03a8-4502-5010-997b-9943e254395b","120":"instance--cefe62ac-5b6e-5ead-84fc-b4c632913a73","150":"instance--4d07a740-2467-5b95-ac8d-4a2ee8edd11e","180":"instance--1205f03c-a457-5a0b-87ef-3bbb7aac110f","210":"instance--96e7dc6a-9f86-5f69-8d45-a566303cd4c0","240":"instance--66237af6-bb19-5a51-9fa2-cbc4a96186f5","270":"instance--836dfd42-b475-50ca-9acf-4f11bd32b89f","30":"instance--efe92997-cc5c-538a-90bc-c09ffb1379f4","300":"instance--9c4a24ae-1426-5cb5-9d7c-792e6dd325b7","330":"instance--06c6a74a-ca7d-5703-88ea-a06a0933d21a","60":"instance--5e4f84e5-56b7-5b8f-9bc3-b4d59d371123","90":"instance--019deb6a-bab3-57db-9a53-11e3564bf7a4"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--2","properties":[["name","Request TGS tickets"],["description","This attack involves requesting a Kerberos service ticket(s) (TGS) for the Service Principal Name (SPN) of the target service account. This request uses a valid domain user\u2019s authentication ticket (TGT) to request one or several service tickets for a target service running on a server. The Domain Controller doesn\u2019t track if the user ever actually connects to these resources (or even if the user has access). The Domain Controller looks up the SPN in Active Directory and encrypts the ticket using the service account associated with the SPN in order for the service to validate user access. The encryption type of the requested Kerberos service ticket is RC4_HMAC_MD5 which means the service account\u2019s NTLM password hash is used to encrypt the service ticket."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0006","technique":"T1558.003"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--0ce35aea-35a2-52ae-a67b-985306bdefe7","120":"instance--312639d5-e6d9-57b1-850d-28f0a1eac2f6","150":"instance--9551a25e-2558-512e-9894-dd64a8d662bf","180":"instance--403becce-e0ad-5dcd-bc14-7c00453907da","210":"instance--2305f501-2712-5ec6-9d4e-1371b011e937","240":"instance--cf1b8cf6-1cbd-5afb-b653-aa693889dab5","270":"instance--1d3dc59a-40a0-5670-aa3e-1304ff762003","30":"instance--77063d4f-503a-5e9b-b622-15aa2cc6a8e7","300":"instance--beaab67f-8a54-5982-8c5d-9d2ed2d42c9f","330":"instance--4d3274ff-ef14-5a53-99be-01575194a98e","60":"instance--4154a6bf-290b-5fce-a557-5dc0f3e700fb","90":"instance--2992bc0b-df57-54e5-a17b-03a964338c09"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--3","properties":[["name","Export TGS tickets from memory"],["description","An attacker can crack service account passwords without ever getting admin access to the server or the network. The attacker gets a foothold on a computer & Requests TGS tickets for several services with service accounts. Exports the TGS tickets from memory, saves them to files, & uploads to a website or webservice (Google Drive)."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0009","technique":"T1005"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--0f6e4da7-a5f4-54d7-866f-3bc6e8bcb019","120":"instance--015254b5-0906-577e-b3e3-3899f837d118","150":"instance--f7af5b8c-330a-58d5-b0da-a3d5f0bc6ad0","180":"instance--9f27ab21-2382-567d-b022-74ad5a29bd08","210":"instance--d799eb0a-7600-5b1a-a298-c47a78ceae4b","240":"instance--911c2c52-5974-5e08-b0b6-a9084d57c6ee","270":"instance--286444b4-97a1-58cd-9ca3-cffa04a15351","30":"instance--92192c38-5143-50e0-8c39-a96ea86e32e2","300":"instance--82bb3de0-bea5-5651-a1de-583283258c6d","330":"instance--4f0945c8-f644-50ce-8796-fea52a29dda1","60":"instance--16c43a2d-7356-521d-a507-5922e2c3337b","90":"instance--abce5c62-339a-5ed5-a0b8-dd66136cfe2f"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--4","properties":[["name","Upload ticket files to web service"],["description","An attacker can crack service account passwords without ever getting admin access to the server or the network. The attacker gets a foothold on a computer & Requests TGS tickets for several services with service accounts. Exports the TGS tickets from memory, saves them to files, & uploads to a website or webservice (Google Drive)."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0010","technique":"T1567"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--a469636c-0cb2-50b9-92f9-644c8aa98197","120":"instance--d57b3a21-e910-5879-8148-40165cea451a","150":"instance--58250ef4-5bb4-5bf3-b33e-89493bbb395d","180":"instance--3e769cf2-c1e5-5d2e-81d4-892f48ce4d86","210":"instance--f6499e41-749c-5d7f-9346-96c08d0d5dfd","240":"instance--d9dcdfc8-5f42-546a-803a-0efcd5d4cf91","270":"instance--c9afd0f6-97ce-57b2-9d60-3557b6214809","30":"instance--75f82155-f5ff-5619-8bf8-aae22937cab0","300":"instance--25e2d26e-1b35-56bd-b9aa-096c2d3b0e3c","330":"instance--e0483688-da10-5376-8cf2-050bcc3b70f0","60":"instance--1293d9cc-16b2-5c67-a453-bd144aab133a","90":"instance--2b43cd52-10db-5b15-8ad5-c4b59496528b"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--5","properties":[["name","Sniff RC4 TGS tickets off the wire"],["description","Note that this attack can also work by sniffing network traffic and grabbing Kerberos TGS tickets encrypted using RC4_HMAC_MD5 off the wire."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0006","technique":"T1040"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--54fc1f38-f4e3-523e-b07c-73889b0d8df7","120":"instance--9cf45948-7040-5d7a-a1d5-3cb4db0c1af6","150":"instance--13bb13cc-e02b-51d2-8d7d-40e5613b6e5a","180":"instance--e33bc6ee-771e-54fe-a772-74dfdaad420d","210":"instance--286f51a3-8fc6-55ec-978e-8b05ebda3655","240":"instance--14659696-be77-5460-beb1-4b5eac126e43","270":"instance--f48ed1a6-2895-5cd2-9b1c-e30ac2bc8921","30":"instance--7b803e61-16ac-5720-92cd-8f2a456a52b7","300":"instance--76c24361-5143-5c43-8e4d-707c619e6038","330":"instance--f395cfc7-395a-5001-9552-a4fec6dbc53a","60":"instance--760885bb-9294-5a5b-93a2-a410e1ea4112","90":"instance--8e0d1a12-8611-598d-9a7d-40f2525e4781"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--6","properties":[["name","Crack service account password offline"],["description","This means that Kerberoast can attempt to open the Kerberos ticket by trying different NTLM hashes and when the ticket is successfully opened, the correct service account password is discovered."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0006","technique":"T1110.002"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--7cccbcd0-a724-54fb-be4f-ac523d26f7d0","120":"instance--738e44b2-1357-5eb3-82bd-8a0ce8942b72","150":"instance--d31f4735-6339-5929-8d7c-d30863cf166f","180":"instance--2252393d-d801-5931-ad38-4b53374a9880","210":"instance--065b5ad5-023a-5336-b458-e9c9dcda2976","240":"instance--5ea0dd2b-5eac-51f8-855a-4cbcb801bc2d","270":"instance--bba66874-a069-56c6-bb95-967cb3cefc9e","30":"instance--6377c09d-ecb4-5567-a2f4-4dde56ff4f98","300":"instance--ede3430f-b16b-58ae-be71-1d1f1a194336","330":"instance--7772f482-8ee2-569a-b600-7528c065d4e0","60":"instance--98139a98-16b0-54fe-8c77-3473c1b520cd","90":"instance--5cb9cc95-e190-5a68-985d-0a94d39299e6"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--7","properties":[["name","Use compromised service account"],["description","The attacker now knows the service account username and password valid on a server (or servers) and likely has administrator rights."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0004","technique":"T1078"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--35652c79-2c41-5d60-81ba-b5e47aa554bf","120":"instance--53906203-fffb-5af3-b112-44a9b4b49b8f","150":"instance--465fbc8a-7b4c-569f-be00-c0fbc137fcfc","180":"instance--a653c96b-3673-5dfa-968e-188fffe4cc04","210":"instance--6a344cf5-bd5c-52db-84f5-23c7701c7a5e","30":"instance--913561d1-b5f3-54d2-8272-159233dfde54","330":"instance--d59fe52d-c897-5f3a-919a-c2273cb8a8b3","60":"instance--f1fd6a3d-bb83-543d-a379-39d4632978f7","90":"instance--4cd6fce2-0d24-57f0-b161-12a867cd1100","branch:False":"instance--f7e897b3-3607-5ea5-8d15-5f83ba8a60da","branch:True":"instance--39b5ac19-b0dd-5674-a7d9-d75e659fe9ea"},"id":"condition","instance":"attack-condition--1","properties":[["description","Once the attacker has a list of Service Principal Names (SPNs) associated with service accounts, these SPNs can be used to request Kerberos TGS service tickets useful for offline TGS password cracking."]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--2ff8b105-17d8-5bc8-9736-a71ca9281068","120":"instance--fe9b11f7-9a07-51c8-93b2-02f34148833b","150":"instance--15f0676c-2f2f-58cf-99a3-b5eade2d286e","180":"instance--cdc5e3d9-a0b4-5995-98a3-d1a29532ffb1","210":"instance--75ed5df8-ff2f-5667-9748-b8587a1ee318","30":"instance--46009917-4258-54e5-9e91-c46c4a45d34d","330":"instance--54845373-a5f0-5af0-b348-5b0a3b4fbe67","60":"instance--f1f8d9a5-1f2a-55c4-af9a-f2629bc0827a","90":"instance--ddfb6e54-4af9-5771-910f-b4c7ba6e9860","branch:False":"instance--64607b7d-a4bd-56e7-9116-7bc21201c8bf","branch:True":"instance--f635d174-aa29-531f-b9c8-0cc481c6c1dd"},"id":"condition","instance":"attack-condition--2","properties":[["description","This request uses a valid domain user\u2019s authentication ticket (TGT) to request one or several service tickets for a target service running on a server."]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--64fa8274-9976-53b9-811c-a0e7e805b799","120":"instance--ce384754-4013-5515-ac17-4456e1d80bbb","150":"instance--99275651-db0d-57ec-a13c-6e557a4b9c7c","180":"instance--cbaa25ac-4f14-51f0-9962-f76fe36e7cd6","210":"instance--1c4fda5b-4605-5040-a88a-48f1df4144aa","30":"instance--39743932-1858-5655-a859-b27c0902b87a","330":"instance--c116df79-3c10-5931-96ec-25b4174ae13a","60":"instance--75b926aa-d189-5cd6-bc7b-5a947c88de41","90":"instance--4931e63d-9e52-5183-bbd8-7db1814b0f21","branch:False":"instance--fc00a7ae-0a9a-58b7-b24a-5def4ea9feab","branch:True":"instance--e3424864-637f-5b96-b87c-a8dcc22d8b9e"},"id":"condition","instance":"attack-condition--3","properties":[["description","when the ticket is successfully opened, the correct service account password is discovered."]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--36aad375-d405-5e3b-9a7d-4346c75c9f45","120":"instance--acc72955-e581-59b3-80b5-35fb047df4b8","150":"instance--d5d0ec7c-da1b-5d39-86e4-8de8792ab05d","180":"instance--047e7862-d9c4-5716-b778-899a86595b48","210":"instance--650a6d3c-5cb0-5f82-83ec-c5d828e2502b","240":"instance--3f08654d-fd5e-59cb-af47-8bbcee29de39","270":"instance--e175549d-38ff-5527-bdb8-de5e1a12f356","30":"instance--c6e60459-b005-50cd-9e68-66ef210b5456","300":"instance--f90b34f0-8620-5a56-9e11-4db2b889aac4","330":"instance--93872aee-cf81-52fa-aa93-f7a84a833dbd","60":"instance--5a877a06-3649-5bba-9461-5faee75ea842","90":"instance--68af6616-0e27-5395-b4ff-5d95b55a2405"},"id":"OR_operator","instance":"attack-operator--1","properties":[["operator","OR"]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--905f37ff-524a-522a-8685-08b6df9b34bd","120":"instance--a0b8bf42-8310-53d9-87f0-390378638ae9","150":"instance--ffafa2fa-6430-5714-9c5e-bbf977c9819b","180":"instance--10bf0e4d-ac4d-5742-b82b-398ef2467e2a","210":"instance--f2066b53-6fa4-5efa-8f61-dc81d3df5b0e","240":"instance--fbb6b151-c9f4-5cb6-b467-c563cc0c60d3","270":"instance--451ff5e8-5cc8-5d6c-b701-da17c04936f7","30":"instance--059bc992-da53-5d4b-ac82-60cfacc08e81","300":"instance--1d241382-a8ee-554a-aa3a-04366535b315","330":"instance--8a7078e9-787d-56b2-a734-f93cd76b3dc8","60":"instance--8aab1831-f6e3-582d-8f9b-3ad920a40e35","90":"instance--192458e5-76c8-5d8c-ab54-9ed8b36ef2bd"},"id":"software","instance":"software--1","properties":[["value","Service Principal Names (SPNs)"],["evidence",[["item-1",{"excerpt":"Once the attacker has a list of Service Principal Names (SPNs) associated with service accounts, these SPNs can be used to request Kerberos TGS service tickets useful for offline TGS password cracking.","source":"https://adsecurity.org/?p=2293"}]]],["display_name","Service Principal Names (SPNs)"],["name","Service Principal Names (SPNs)"]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--cba0db2f-4c26-5332-99c5-b2aee8fd787f","120":"instance--d8fb103f-8665-5f80-9047-210dfff8d4c0","150":"instance--edc40449-4888-59a1-9397-f5c8d35412fc","180":"instance--4252ed4d-ac52-5ce9-b1de-22e62358c57f","210":"instance--ef2d806c-0b9d-5611-a51f-36bdd082998e","240":"instance--ec0c67c0-158e-5415-b08b-15c497764894","270":"instance--a848e595-3d48-563d-8a20-94fb272a5c7a","30":"instance--3c5974dd-03ad-5327-9c64-210b94c5a53b","300":"instance--276d1f29-b75a-59cc-9eed-4b08918a5156","330":"instance--890f4571-fa81-56df-b189-618233836d08","60":"instance--2dd9e3f9-0428-53d4-807b-4d5e12c46854","90":"instance--caf97c38-c923-57ff-b66b-316622e455c9"},"id":"user_account","instance":"user-account--1","properties":[["user_id","valid domain user"],["account_type","domain"],["evidence",[["item-1",{"excerpt":"This request uses a valid domain user\u2019s authentication ticket (TGT) to request one or several service tickets for a target service running on a server.","source":"https://adsecurity.org/?p=2293"}]]],["display_name","valid domain user"]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--ef7d9494-2264-5606-9719-07e3a5cc9395","120":"instance--ff321850-6f13-5372-b1ef-f3279fced335","150":"instance--78c7fb7e-3084-5e08-ba7f-ea68de55bf2b","180":"instance--b4de8f7f-abde-55e6-bab3-4a0d78a6719a","210":"